component inpos_motion """Count servo cycles in which a joint moves although motion reports it in position.

A cycle counts when in-position was TRUE in the previous cycle, is still
TRUE, and the watched position changed: the machine moving on after it was
reported at rest. The cycle a move starts (in-position falls with it) and
the cycle it arrives (in-position rises with it) do not count. Counted in
the servo thread, so the result does not depend on when a test looks.
Steps below 1e-9 do not count: a mode switch hands the position from one
planner to another with a rounding step of ~1e-16.""";

pin in  bit   inpos  "motion.in-position";
pin in  float pos    "Watched position (joint motor position command)";
pin out s32   count  "Cycles moved while reported in position";

variable int was = 1;
variable double last = 0;
variable int primed = 0;

function _;
license "GPL";
;;

#include <math.h>


if (primed && was && inpos && fabs(pos - last) > 1e-9)
    count++;
was = inpos;
last = pos;
primed = 1;
